Divide unit results (32/32 and 64/32) follow the SH7604 manual and Ymir's hardware-tested divider:
0x80000000 / -1 saturates and flags overflow; a 64/32 quotient of exactly 2^31 with a zero remainder
fits when the divisor's sign allows it, every other out-of-range quotient overflows, and on overflow
the unit has run three steps of its partial division (DVDNTH, and DVDNTL when the overflow interrupt
is enabled). Includes what was 016-divider-ymir-edge-cases. Upstream 6b2d640ce keeps the former
results for speed on ARM32; on aarch64 a 64-bit divide is one instruction.

